  "contract": "Pinned worker selects the last query row for each real ordinary request and the last 1+drafts consecutive rows when verifying. The historical config and client are hash matched to the ordinary run. Engine counters cover one successful request per active DP and stage; graph counts can also include the other DP.",
  "scope": [
    "Six trace-sized requests; no individual logits index payload from this run. Initial one-row projection assumes a prompt step without drafts. Preserve prompt logprobs when requested and pre-layer draft auxiliary states. Other final raw readers can keep the last FFN dense.",
    "Keeping contiguous owners and equal packets, any six consecutive rows still use 24 fixed slots. Moving rows to at least six owners permits eight slots, with at least 3 or 4 rows changing owner depending on the initial alignment. Changing ownership or using ragged exchanges has costs not priced here.",
    "Same-size bank or packet does not imply zero local savings. Other rank experts, routing, KV state and raw rows are separate dependencies. No wall-clock speedup measured. Mixed arrivals, cache residence, overlap and new packing can change the credited time."
  ],
